FIXTURE CONTROL
  test/fixture_roots/complexity_accumulator_copy/clean_linear.dag
  expected TSV standing: scanned  0  0

POPULATION
  relay/arrow-census/arrow-form-files.txt
  520 paths, sorted UTF-8 byte order, under dag/ and src/v2, produced by:
  f: ( ... =>  inside 400 chars, after stripping f: fn(
  (520 on 5f931fcc92a; the ~518 figure was the same heuristic on origin/main.)

BATCH 1 SLICE
  relay/arrow-census/batch1-slice.txt
  = fixture + first 16 lines of arrow-form-files.txt  (17 paths)

PER-FILE COMMAND (cwd = arm-root)
  $GUNBC run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 \
    --entry src/v2/lens/complexity_accumulator_copy/corpus_census.dag \
    --function census_tsv_line_for_path \
    --arg path=<relative-path>

TSV CAPTURE
  census_tsv_line_for_path returns String, not ProcessExit. gunbc exits 2 and prints:
    error: function `census_tsv_line_for_path` returned `<LINE>`, not `ProcessExit`.
  <LINE> is:
    <path>	scanned	<suspects>	<refusals>
    or
    <path>	not_established	<cause>	0
  Extract with: returned `(.*)`, not `ProcessExit`

RUN A SLICE
  bash relay/arrow-census/run-slice.sh <arm-root> <file-list-slice> <out-dir>
  Each file: systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=16G -p RuntimeMaxSec=1200
             /usr/bin/time -v <per-file command>
  First file in the slice reads /sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max inside the scope (written once to out-dir/memory.max.readback).
  Appends one TSV row per file to out-dir/runs.tsv
  Columns: path	reason	wall_sec	cpu_user_sec	cpu_sys_sec	max_rss_kb	status	tsv
  reason is one of: ok | suspect | timeout | oom | other

  Parallelism 8 is the caller's job (split the slice, 8 invocations, or xargs -P 8 wrapping
  single-path slices). This script is one slice, sequential, so MemoryMax readback is unambiguous.

JOIN
